.el .ds Aq '
.TH cadcraft-cli-roundtrip 1  "roundtrip " 
.SH NAME
cadcraft\-cli\-roundtrip \- Open each DXF/DWG, save it as DXF and DWG, reopen and compare; writes report.md and report.json
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcadcraft\-cli roundtrip\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-saved\fR] [\fB\-\-same\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-census\fR] [\fB\-\-tolerance\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIFILE|FOLDER\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open each DXF/DWG, save it as DXF and DWG, reopen and compare; writes report.md and report.json
.PP
FOLDER defaults to $CADCRAFT_CORPUS_DIR. With CADCRAFT_CORPUS_STRICT=1 it fails when a file doesn\*(Aqt open, save or reopen, or loses records on save.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Where the report goes (default: `report` beside the files)
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-saved\fR
Keep the saved files, in `saved` under the report folder
.TP
\fB\-\-same\-format\fR
Save only in each file\*(Aqs own format
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-census\fR
Don\*(Aqt count what each file holds (faster; no "read lost" column)
.TP
\fB\-\-tolerance\fR \fI<T>\fR [default: 0.000001]
How far numbers may move and still count as equal
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIFILE|FOLDER\fR]
A drawing, or a folder of them
